# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Original game data is COPYRIGHTED and must never be committed.
# The engine loads these at runtime from the user's own copy of Tubes.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.EXE
*.exe
*.RES
*.res
*.SAV
*.sav
# The player's high score table, and the text-mode screens the archive carries.
# `*.SAV` was here from the start and `*.HSC` was not, which is an accident of
# which file the port learned to write first - both are the player's.
*.HSC
*.hsc
*.BIN
*.bin
*.DOC
*.doc
*.CFG
*.cfg
CATALOG.TXT
ORDERFRM.DOC

# Extracted assets are derived works of the above - also never committed.
assets-extracted/
*.unpacked
*.dump

# Build output
build/
build-*/
*.o
*.a
compile_commands.json

# Session transcripts the assistant harness drops in the working directory.
# They are working notes, not the record - docs/worklog.md is the record.
# Two harnesses, two naming schemes: Claude Code dates them, Opencode uses the
# session id and Markdown.
20[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-*.txt
session-ses_*.md

# One machine's paths to the game directory, the Ghidra project and the
# tooling checkout. CLAUDE.md is tracked and names none of them.
CLAUDE.local.md

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
